## Branch And Worktree Policy

- Canonical local branches are pickup points unless this project says otherwise.
- Use task branches or task worktrees for mutable work when a task may span
  repos, run codegen, change deploy inputs, or need runtime QA.
- Preserve unrelated dirty files and user changes.

## Landing Policy

- For single-repo work, land after that repo passes its documented gates.
- For cross-repo work, use all-or-hold landing unless a slice explicitly says
  otherwise.

## Deploy Authority

- Deployment requires an explicit deploy trigger from the user or this project's
  `DEPLOY.md`.
